How to create a file?
touch fileName

How to check the permission of a file in linux?
ls -l fileName
returns: -rw-rw-r--
First character means if its a file or folder
- means regular file
next 3 permission for owner, permission for group, permission for others
Owner can read and write, group can read and write and others can only read

how to check the permission of a folder in linux?
ls -ld fileName
returns: drwxrwxr-x
d means directory
owner can read, write, execute
group can read, write, execute
others can only read and execute

4 = read
2 = write
1 = execute

How to override file permission
chmod 777 fileName 

How to check if a system is exist or not?
systemctl list-unit-files | grep rabbitmq

How to check the status of a service?
systemctl status ssh

How to start a service?
systemctl start ssh

How to stop a service?
systemctl stop ssh

How to configure a service which will enable when the system boot up?
sudo systemctl enable service-name

How to configure a service which remain disable when the system boot up?
sudo systemctl disable service-name


How to restart a service?
sudo systemctl restart service-name


Where to check all the  system configuration?
cd /etc/systemd/system

How to install any software?
sudo apt install nginx


How to see the system dashboard?
top

How to see all process with details?
ps aux

How to see a specific process with details?
ps aux | grep processname

How to see how much disk space is available?
df -h

How to check the size of specific directory?
du -sh folder path (du -sh /var/log)

How to see which service runs on which port?
netstat -tulpn / ss -tulpn

How to see which service runs on 80 port?
netstat -tulpn | grep :80

Problem: Your web server is running slowly.

# 1. Check overall system load
top

# 2. See if your web server process is running
ps aux | grep nginx

# 3. Check if you're running out of disk space for logs
df -h /var/log

# 4. Check how big the log files have grown
du -sh /var/log/nginx/

# 5. Check if the web server is listening on the correct port
netstat -tulpn | grep :80
# or
ss -tulpn | grep :80

# 6. Check active connections to your web server
netstat -tupn | grep nginx


How to connect a server using ssh
ssh -p portNumber userName@dns

Signal	Number	Purpose	Common Use
SIGTERM	15	Terminate gracefully	Ask nicely to shut down
SIGKILL	9	Terminate immediately	Force kill, no cleanup
SIGHUP	1	Hang up	Reload configuration
SIGSTOP	17,19,23	Pause execution	Freeze a process
SIGCONT	19,18,25	Continue execution	Resume a paused process

How to kill a process?
kill -15 processId
kill -9 processId

How to advance process kill?
pkill processName (pkill firefox)

How to see logs in a log file?
tail -f fileName

How to see a service log?
journalctl -u serviceName

How to check disk usage?
df -h | grep -v tmpfs

How to check memory usage?
free -h














